    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="top" type="adressline"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3352"
                            type="person">Miss Mary Watson</rs><lb/>Bureau of Occupations,
                        Inc.<lb/>1776 Broadway<lb/><rs ref="#tillich_place_id__319" type="place">New
                            York</rs> 19, <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__865" type="place">N.
                        Y.</rs></fw><dateline><date when="1946-03-12">March 12,
                        1946</date></dateline><salute>Dear <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3352"
                            type="person">Miss Watson</rs>:</salute>
                </opener>
                <p>I have known <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3339" type="person">Mrs. Hilde
                        Frankel</rs> for many years since I was acquainted with her family in <rs
                        ref="#tillich_place_id__143" type="place">Frankfurt aM</rs> before I left
                        <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__122" type="place">Germany</rs>. She comes from a
                    highly educated family and has worked in this country in different humanitarian
                    committees and at the same time as my personal secretary. She is absolutely
                    reliable, <del rend="s">absolutely</del> understanding in all social problems
                    and an indefatigable worker. She is one of the few people whom I can recommend
                    without restrictions.</p>
                <closer><salute>Yours sincerely,</salute><signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928"
                            type="person">Prof. Paul Tillich</rs>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
